DevSecOps Interview Questions You Should Be Ready For 🔐
 Whether you're preparing for a role or evaluating your current practices, these questions dive deep into the real-world challenges of secure cloud-native delivery.

💡 DevSecOps & Security Integration
How do you implement shift-left security in a CI/CD pipeline?
How do you integrate tools like Snyk or Aqua Security into build workflows?
How do you manage secrets securely across environments (Vault, AWS Secrets Manager)?
What’s your approach for generating and validating SBOMs?
What are key cultural aspects of DevSecOps?
How do SAST, DAST, and IAST differ?
How are you implementing SCA in your environment?
What do you understand by RASP?
What’s the difference between white-box, black-box, and grey-box testing?

☁️ Cloud Infrastructure & IaC
How do you design multi-cloud architecture using Terraform or Pulumi?
What are the key differences in managing infra across AWS, Azure, and GCP?
How have you used IaC to enforce compliance/security policies?
How do you handle DR and high availability in cloud-native setups?

🚀 CI/CD & Automation
Describe your experience with GitHub Actions, Jenkins, or ArgoCD.
How do you ensure security and compliance in automated deployments?
What challenges have you faced with GitOps workflows?
How do you integrate DAST/SAST tools into CI/CD?

🐳 Containers & Kubernetes
How do you manage Helm charts and Operators in production?
What’s your experience with service meshes like Istio or Linkerd?
How do you secure Kubernetes clusters across cloud providers?
How do you troubleshoot performance issues in Kubernetes?

📊 Monitoring & Observability
How do you design observability stacks using Prometheus, Grafana, OpenTelemetry?
What’s your approach to root cause analysis?
How do you ensure visibility across microservices?
Share a time when monitoring helped prevent a major outage.

🧠 Programming & Scripting
Which scripting language do you prefer for automation and why?
Share a script/tool you built to improve DevSecOps workflows.
How do you handle error logging in automation scripts?
What’s your approach to writing secure code in Python/Go/Java?

🧩 Architecture & Design Thinking
How do you balance scalability, security, and cost-efficiency?
Describe a system you designed with cross-functional collaboration.
How do you evaluate and select tools for DevSecOps initiatives?
What’s your approach to continuous improvement in platform engineering?
